    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "There is no formula to compute with. The student must interpret f(f(x))=x as an involution and apply it to the given point: f(5)=f(f(2))=2, so (5,2) is on the graph. This is a single unsignposted step, and it requires moving between function notation and points on a graph. That makes it more demanding than the direct composition evaluations in p15-q8. Once the idea is seen there is no algebra, so it is slightly easier than the multi-step simplification with domain exclusions in p16-q12.",
